WEBVTT

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.490
Straight ahead, straight ahead!

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:15.780
Not bad, Chiaki!

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.580
Not "that" way, more towards "that" way.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:21.750
Where is "that" way?

00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:24.690
Chiaki! Here!

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.630
Go for it, Chiaki-chan.

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:32.820
Eat this, you fool!

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:40.480
Here.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:41.700
Thanks.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:00:56.480
Ok, thanks for all the hard work yesterday.

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:58.740
Thanks for all the hard work.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:00.080
Here, please help yourself.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:01.780
Alright!

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:03.710
Thank you very much.

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:06.700
It was really tiring.

00:01:06.700 --> 00:01:10.440
All because Takeru took about 4 hours to get to the beach.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.590
We were fine with it.

00:01:12.590 --> 00:01:16.400
But for Kana-chan it must have been pretty hard.

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.720
She got really carsick.

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:24.850
I thought I was the kind that wouldn't get carsick.

00:01:32.110 --> 00:01:35.610
Damn you, Takeru...

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:38.560
Go for it! Kana-chan!

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:40.900
Just a little bit more...

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:42.410
Sea...

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:45.910
Still, you really wanted to swim.

00:01:45.910 --> 00:01:49.210
You looked like a turtle returning to sea.

00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:53.890
Takeru is really useless when it comes to crucial matters.

00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:56.510
I feel like hitting him.

00:01:56.510 --> 00:01:58.120
Now now...

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:02.010
In return, we followed Kana-chan's orders and buried your uncle.

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:04.750
Bury the idiot!

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:06.020
Roger!

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:08.970
Oh dear, what to do...

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:12.680
That uncle's true identity is your cousin, right?

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:14.380
A brother?

00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:15.780
I don't really care...

00:02:15.780 --> 00:02:17.660
Speaking of brothers.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:20.870
Here you are.

00:02:20.870 --> 00:02:22.640
Thank you very much.

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:26.580
Fujioka and Chiaki are like siblings.

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:29.370
This... how do I put it...

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:34.160
Siblings... that's impossible.

00:02:34.160 --> 00:02:37.160
Uchida is really weird.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:39.640
Eh? Where's Chiaki?

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.910
She said she was looking for something.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:43.550
I see.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:46.540
Hey, Kana.

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:49.060
Where did you put Fujioka?

00:02:51.180 --> 00:02:53.020
I don't know if you know this but,

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:56.910
the Fujioka that Chiaki is talking about is her favourite stuffed toy.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.880
You don't need to explain.

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:01.070
It was you again, right?

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:02.660
Quickly, return it to me.

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.850
This time it isn't me.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:05.580
Eh?

00:03:05.580 --> 00:03:08.700
You took it to the beach, right?

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:10.670
Didn't you forget it and leave it there?

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:13.420
I brought it there but...

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:15.630
I didn't take it out.

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:19.240
Huh? But I saw Fujioka there.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:20.270
At the sea?

00:03:20.270 --> 00:03:23.220
Yeah. There were other witnesses.

00:03:28.370 --> 00:03:31.630
Erm, does Chiaki-chan like this?

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:32.690
Eh?

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:40.150
You dumbass!

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:50.790
Yep, she uses it every day.

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:53.070
I see.

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:55.590
Use?

00:03:56.340 --> 00:03:58.660
There was a conversation like that.

00:03:58.660 --> 00:04:00.520
See, you left it there.

00:04:00.520 --> 00:04:01.430
Eh?

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:04.730
It must be floating out to sea by now.

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:06.130
No way...

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.640
Someone is here.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:10.100
Here.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.840
I found this inside my bag.

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:18.980
It was put in Fujioka's bag?

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:22.410
Why did Fujioka steal Fujioka?

00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:24.640
I didn't steal it.

00:04:24.640 --> 00:04:27.820
But, I don't remember putting it in my bag.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:31.450
Chiaki! Hurry up!

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:32.720
Oh!

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.960
I feel sick!

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:39.170
Don't vomit in my bag!

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:44.600
Chiaki! Hurry up!

00:04:44.600 --> 00:04:46.740
I am coming!

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:50.680
Wait! Chiaki!

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:59.280
And so, I left it with all the bags.

00:04:59.280 --> 00:05:03.950
Someone else put it in Fujioka's bag, then.

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:09.810
Kana-chan, hurry up!

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:11.150
We are going to change!

00:05:11.150 --> 00:05:12.590
Ok!

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:17.700
That Chiaki, she brought this here.

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:20.510
It can't be helped, if she forgets it, it would be bad.

00:05:20.510 --> 00:05:22.470
Let me put it away.

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:33.810
Ah!

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:39.930
I see, it was my fault.

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:42.070
But If I say that, I'll probably get scolded.

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:45.990
Kana, what was with that "ah"?

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:48.240
Eh? Ah!

00:06:01.220 --> 00:06:02.630
I love you!

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:07.220
That's it.

00:06:07.220 --> 00:06:11.390
To be able to meet all of you, you are all so outstanding.

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:19.950
What kind of reaction do you want?

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:21.860
I hope this will pass.

00:06:24.620 --> 00:06:26.090
All the way till the opposite shore...

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:11.200
Hey, Haruka!

00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:13.140
Let's take a break!

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:17.800
No way. Didn't you want me to "teach you how to do summer homework"?

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:20.640
Yes, I did say that but...

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:25.530
See! Someone is here, Haruka!

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:26.920
It's fine.

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:28.700
Kana, please.

00:08:31.620 --> 00:08:33.490
I brought a watermelon.

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:35.320
Oh, that's great!

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:38.450
Everyone! It's a watermelon.

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:40.070
That's great!

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:41.360
It's really big!

00:08:41.360 --> 00:08:43.450
Thank you very much, Fujioka-kun.

00:08:43.450 --> 00:08:45.000
It's not a big deal.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.130
Hello.

00:08:46.130 --> 00:08:48.360
Hi there.

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:50.170
Hey, come over here.

00:08:50.170 --> 00:08:51.710
Yes?

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:54.130
It looks tasty.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:57.780
I just felt like eating watermelon.

00:08:57.780 --> 00:09:00.170
But didn't you just eat some recently?

00:09:00.170 --> 00:09:02.230
Watermelon is the best for summer days.

00:09:03.180 --> 00:09:05.270
Watermelon-sama, watermelon-sama!

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:08.110
The watermelon is going to get hot.

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:15.460
You planned to get on Kana's good side by bringing such a nice food present, right?

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:18.690
Plan? Something like that... I...

00:09:18.690 --> 00:09:21.500
Don't hide it! I can see it.

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:28.820
It's best to cut the watermelon into slices like this.

00:09:28.820 --> 00:09:31.420
Or else there isn't that "eating watermelon" feeling.

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:33.300
Yep.

00:09:35.340 --> 00:09:36.630
That spoon.

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:39.220
Doesn't Kana-chan use it often?

00:09:45.820 --> 00:09:47.810
Touma, let's compete to see who can finish it faster!

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:49.610
What did you say? I won't lose to you.

00:09:54.530 --> 00:09:56.910
Kana, did you just spit a seed at me?

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:58.490
It wasn't me.

00:10:01.070 --> 00:10:02.950
Stop it. It's dirty.

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:04.870
It isn't dirty.

00:10:04.870 --> 00:10:07.970
Touma, that wasn't any challenge.

00:10:07.970 --> 00:10:10.880
That was dirty, you took advantage and finished eating.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:13.050
Kana, that wasn't nice manners.

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:16.090
Damn, I was spotted. How embarrassing.

00:10:16.090 --> 00:10:18.060
But speaking of manners,

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:20.600
Fujioka was gobbling down food.

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:24.600
Hey, I took out the spoon, please use it.

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:32.730
Maki-chan, Fujioka.

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:34.360
What is it, Minami?

00:10:34.360 --> 00:10:36.590
Are you going to eat here?

00:10:36.590 --> 00:10:37.830
Of course!

00:10:37.830 --> 00:10:40.080
You always eat here!

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:41.390
What about you, Maki-chan?

00:10:41.390 --> 00:10:42.080
Ok.

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:44.100
What about you?

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:45.440
Can I?

00:10:45.440 --> 00:10:46.580
Of course.

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:47.750
Ok.

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:51.590
Since that's decided, should I make curry tonight?

00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:55.230
Haruka will be Maki-chan's teacher.

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:58.110
Really? That would be a big help.

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:00.600
Ok.

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:02.300
Let's get busy.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:05.260
Kana, you must hide the hidden flavour properly.

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:06.890
I know.

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:11.080
When hiding the flavour, you shouldn't just add a lot of it.

00:11:11.080 --> 00:11:14.140
I know.

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:16.860
Chiaki.

00:11:16.860 --> 00:11:19.210
Don't hide the carrots.

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:25.790
I added carrots as the hidden flavour today.

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:28.970
Then hide them.

00:11:28.970 --> 00:11:30.670
The carrots are huge.

00:11:38.760 --> 00:11:41.070
Oh Fujioka. Wait a moment.

00:11:41.070 --> 00:11:42.260
What is it, Minami?

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:43.220
Here, you can have this.

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:46.030
It's a spoon for guests.

00:11:46.030 --> 00:11:47.630
It was put over here.

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:52.180
The guest and host spoons are separated.

00:11:52.180 --> 00:11:54.980
But, come to think of it, there is no designated spoon for anyone.

00:12:01.990 --> 00:12:04.110
Touma, let's see who can finish it faster.

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:05.200
Another one!

00:13:03.820 --> 00:13:06.550
I don't get it!

00:13:16.020 --> 00:13:17.980
Afternoon...

00:13:17.980 --> 00:13:19.110
Eh?

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:22.880
Haruka... and even Kana aren't here.

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:26.030
Uchida, what are you doing?

00:13:27.710 --> 00:13:30.790
Eh? What's today's date?

00:13:30.790 --> 00:13:32.910
August 31st.

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:37.610
Makoto-ku... Mako-chan, is your summer homework finished?

00:13:37.610 --> 00:13:40.420
No, I completely forgot.

00:13:40.760 --> 00:13:43.300
I completely forgot too.

00:13:43.300 --> 00:13:45.950
I wanted to copy Chiaki's but...

00:13:45.950 --> 00:13:47.970
I was refused.

00:13:47.970 --> 00:13:51.210
Touma seems to have been rejected too.

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:52.930
Touma gave up?

00:13:53.960 --> 00:13:57.450
But I don't want to be scolded by the teacher.

00:13:57.450 --> 00:14:00.580
Ok. Leave it to me, Uchida.

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:02.320
You have a way?

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:05.080
I will try and ask Chiaki...

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:07.930
Ask her to lend you her homework to copy.

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:09.320
Mako-chan!

00:14:09.910 --> 00:14:14.540
But if you get to copy, will you let me copy yours?

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:16.220
Ok.

00:14:16.220 --> 00:14:19.670
But that's if Chiaki lets me copy...

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:23.760
Chiaki, Chiaki.

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:27.280
What is it?

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:30.540
Chiaki... won't you help Uchida?

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:36.860
I thought you might know better since you always come over.

00:14:36.860 --> 00:14:38.900
This summer, Uchida...

00:14:45.350 --> 00:14:47.570
Came over and laughed.

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:54.020
Sorry!

00:14:54.020 --> 00:14:56.500
Came over and cried.
Sorry!

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:56.520
Came over and cried.

00:14:56.710 --> 00:15:01.510
Tasty! Haruka, another bowl please.

00:15:01.510 --> 00:15:02.600
Ok.

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:04.420
Came over and ate.

00:15:04.930 --> 00:15:08.930
But didn't show any sign of coming to do homework!

00:15:08.930 --> 00:15:11.530
As much as I love being depended on by others,

00:15:11.530 --> 00:15:13.720
I hate being a life preserver for others.

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:15.980
Th-that's true.

00:15:15.980 --> 00:15:21.520
Speaking of that, if you really care,
why don't you teach her, Mako-chan?

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:26.630
If it's Mako-chan, elementary school questions should be a piece of cake.

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:31.950
I see. Chiaki thinks that because I am Kana's junior, I am in secondary school.

00:15:33.300 --> 00:15:37.060
And so, I will teach you how to do your homework.

00:15:38.330 --> 00:15:41.100
That's why, let me copy later.

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:43.220
Eh?

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:46.630
That's not right, Chiaki.

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:49.820
Getting an adult to help with a child's homework is...

00:15:49.820 --> 00:15:52.090
Mako-chan, lend me your ear.

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:57.780
I am not a devil.

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:04.320
But if Uchida can reflect on her actions, I'll let her see it.

00:16:07.810 --> 00:16:09.840
Mako-chan.

00:16:09.840 --> 00:16:11.780
Hey, Mako-chan.

00:16:11.780 --> 00:16:14.260
What did Chiaki say?

00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:15.580
Beats me...

00:16:17.370 --> 00:16:19.660
No way...

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:21.260
Uchida.

00:16:22.650 --> 00:16:24.540
Don't blindly copy.

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:26.420
There is bound to be mistakes.

00:16:29.430 --> 00:16:31.260
Thanks, Chiaki!

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:34.890
Makoto-ku... Erm I mean, it's all because of Mako-chan.

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:37.310
Eh? Yeah.

00:16:43.180 --> 00:16:46.750
...Television Shopping~

00:16:50.070 --> 00:16:51.880
There is progress!

00:16:51.880 --> 00:16:53.360
Let me copy it, too!

00:16:53.360 --> 00:16:56.620
You didn't put in any effort and now you
want to copy it? Don't even think about it!

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:59.080
Why? So stingy.

00:17:01.570 --> 00:17:03.230
Mako-chan!

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:05.500
Eh? Me?

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:09.030
What is it, Touma?

00:17:09.030 --> 00:17:12.390
Hey, Makoto. Let me copy after you are done.

00:17:12.390 --> 00:17:15.090
Eh? Umm...

00:17:19.890 --> 00:17:21.100
That's that.

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:24.310
Eh? Why?

00:19:05.150 --> 00:19:07.410
What's the matter, Kana?

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:20.060
What's the matter?

00:19:20.060 --> 00:19:22.950
I can't feel the summer breeze.

00:19:25.490 --> 00:19:27.310
It's already autumn.

00:19:29.020 --> 00:19:32.010
It's almost time for the change of seasonal clothes.

00:19:32.010 --> 00:19:36.240
Okay! For the sake of remembering this past summer, let's try to grab it by its tail.

00:19:51.800 --> 00:19:53.160
Swimsuits!?

00:19:53.160 --> 00:19:55.170
You already changed so stop complaining.

00:19:55.170 --> 00:19:57.230
Why in the bathroom?

00:19:57.230 --> 00:19:59.880
Where else do you want to go in that swimsuit?

00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:04.760
It's already autumn.

00:20:04.760 --> 00:20:06.940
I hate autumn.

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:09.720
If summer were longer it would be good.

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:12.690
What's the matter, Chiaki?

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:16.980
My summer this year was the worst.

00:20:18.740 --> 00:20:20.570
On that summer day.

00:20:23.430 --> 00:20:26.910
The watermelon I had wasn't as good as yours.

00:20:27.500 --> 00:20:29.710
And on another summer day.

00:20:33.740 --> 00:20:37.080
While eating soumen, you put wasabi in it.

00:20:37.540 --> 00:20:39.840
And then another day in the summer.

00:20:41.280 --> 00:20:43.230
It's cola.

00:20:46.480 --> 00:20:49.600
I was tricked into eating soy sauce flavoured shaved ice.

00:20:51.160 --> 00:20:52.900
It was a detestable summer.

00:20:56.360 --> 00:20:59.150
Give me back my summer!

00:21:02.980 --> 00:21:05.850
Well then, what should we eat for dinner.

00:21:09.990 --> 00:21:11.540
Good afternoon.

00:21:11.540 --> 00:21:14.430
This is chestnut rice that my family made.

00:21:14.430 --> 00:21:16.740
Thanks!

00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:19.050
Looks delicious!

00:21:19.050 --> 00:21:20.940
Right?

00:21:23.220 --> 00:21:25.370
Excuse me for the intrusion.

00:21:26.060 --> 00:21:29.200
The fish shop owner gave me some Pacific Saury.

00:21:29.200 --> 00:21:30.400
Splendid.

00:21:30.400 --> 00:21:33.440
What did you use on that fish shop owner?

00:21:34.320 --> 00:21:36.360
Hey!

00:21:36.360 --> 00:21:37.970
I came.

00:21:39.970 --> 00:21:43.980
This is what Natsuki told me to bring when I came over.

00:21:43.980 --> 00:21:45.930
Weird shaped mushrooms.

00:21:45.930 --> 00:21:47.450
Those are Matsutake mushrooms!

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:49.390
Welcome, Touma-sama!

00:21:49.390 --> 00:21:51.920
You've arrived, Touma-sama!

00:21:53.960 --> 00:21:56.650
You guys are here.

00:21:57.250 --> 00:21:59.420
What were the both of you doing?

00:21:59.420 --> 00:22:01.870
Reminiscing about the summer.

00:22:01.870 --> 00:22:04.680
Remembering lots of things...

00:22:04.680 --> 00:22:08.050
Both of you, please look forward to tonight's dinner.

00:22:08.050 --> 00:22:10.230
And please put on some clothes.

00:22:10.230 --> 00:22:11.520
What?

00:22:12.630 --> 00:22:14.390
Matsutake mushrooms!

00:22:14.390 --> 00:22:16.640
Autumn is great!

00:22:23.320 --> 00:22:25.490
There's plenty for everyone.

00:22:25.490 --> 00:22:28.390
Let's eat!

00:22:29.830 --> 00:22:30.890
Eh?

00:22:30.890 --> 00:22:31.950
what's the matter?

00:22:31.950 --> 00:22:34.940
This chestnut rice has no chestnuts.

00:22:34.940 --> 00:22:36.820
That's a surprise.

00:22:36.820 --> 00:22:38.820
Mine has lots.

00:22:38.820 --> 00:22:39.880
Mine too.

00:22:41.500 --> 00:22:43.840
Is it at the bottom?

00:22:47.790 --> 00:22:51.790
Eh? Why is there only grated radish on this plate?

00:22:51.790 --> 00:22:55.460
Don't tell me the fish got up and ran away?

00:22:55.460 --> 00:22:57.440
How could that happen?

00:22:58.060 --> 00:23:00.060
Where's the Matsutake mushrooms?

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:01.970
The Matsutake mushrooms too.

00:23:01.970 --> 00:23:04.980
Where did the Matsutake mushrooms go?

00:23:05.780 --> 00:23:11.700
Matsutake mushrooms aren't something that amateurs can find easily.

00:23:13.640 --> 00:23:16.250
Don't look down on autumn.

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:32.530
Goodbye summer!

00:23:32.530 --> 00:23:35.110
Time really flies when you're having fun.

00:23:35.110 --> 00:23:37.580
I didn't get to play enough.

00:23:37.580 --> 00:23:40.170
Next time on Minami-ke Okaeri.

00:23:40.170 --> 00:23:41.390
If you are fine with me

00:23:41.390 --> 00:23:44.380
It's my season, dumbass.
